[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.EQDSKReader","page":"API","text":"EQDSKReader\n\nProvides functionality to read EQDSK file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.EQDSKReader"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.Content","page":"API","text":"Content\n\nContent of EQDSK file.\n\nAttrs:\n\ncase    identification character string\nnw      number of horizontal grid points\nnh      number of vertical grid points\nrdim    horizontal dimension in metter of computational box\nzdim    vertical dimension in metter of computational box\nrcentr  R in meter of vacuum toroidal magnetic field BCENTR\nrleft   Minimum R in meter of rectangular computational box\nzmid    Z of center of computational box in meter\nrmaxis  R of magnetic axis in meter\nzmaxis  Z of magnetic axis in meter\nsimag   poloidal flux at magnetic axis in Weber /rad\nsibry   poloidal flux at the plasma boundary in Weber /rad\nbcentr  Vacuum toroidal magnetic field in Tesla at RCENTR\ncurrent Plasma current in Ampere\nfpol    Poloidal current function in m-T, F = RB_T on flux grid\npres    Plasma pressure in nt / m^2 on uniform flux grid\nffprim  FF’(ψ) in (mT)^2 / (Weber /rad) on uniform flux grid\npprime  P’(ψ) in (nt/m^2 ) / (Weber /rad) on uniform flux grid\npsirz   Poloidal flux in Weber / rad on the rectangular grid points\nqpsi    q values on uniform flux grid from axis to boundary\nnbbbs   Number of boundary points\nlimitr  Number of limiter points\nrbbbs   R of boundary points in meter\nzbbbs   Z of boundary points in meter\nrlim    R of surrounding limiter contour in meter\nzlim    Z of surrounding limiter contour in mete\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.Content"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.Content-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API","text":"Content(path::AbstractString)\n\nBuild Content object from a file with a in EQDSK format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.Content"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.Content-Tuple{IO}","page":"API","text":"Content(io::IO)\n\nBuild Content object from an input stream with a in EQDSK format.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.Content"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.calc_boundary_psi-Tuple{Content}","page":"API","text":"calc_boundary_psi(c::Content)\n\nReturns average value of ψ at the specified plasma boundary.\n\nThis value is used in normalize_psi.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.calc_boundary_psi"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.create_normalized_psi_interpolator-Tuple{Content}","page":"API","text":"create_normalized_psi_interpolator(c::Content)::Function\n\nReturns function ψ(r,z) where value is 0 at magnetic axis and 1 at plasma boundary\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.create_normalized_psi_interpolator"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.create_psi_interpolator-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"API","text":"create_psi_interpolator(ψ, rpoints, zpoints)\n\nCreate interpolator for matrix ψ with coordinates rpoints and zpoints.\n\nReturns function ψ(r,z) to compute ψ at arbitrary point.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.create_psi_interpolator"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.create_psi_interpolator-Tuple{Content}","page":"API","text":"create_psi_interpolator(c::Content)\n\nCreate ψ  interpolator for Content.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.create_psi_interpolator"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.in_plasma-Tuple{Any, Float64, Float64, Float64}","page":"API","text":"in_plasma(ψ, r, z, separation_z)::Bool\n\nIs point (r,z) in plasma?\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.in_plasma"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.lowest_boundary_point-Tuple{Content}","page":"API","text":"lowest_boundary_point(c::Content)\n\nReturns coordinates of the lowest point at plasma boundary. This is useful to select points in plasma. There should be ψ ≤ 1 and the points are to be above this point.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.lowest_boundary_point"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.normalize_psi-Tuple{Matrix{Float64}, Float64}","page":"API","text":"function normalize_psi(ψ::Matrix{Float64})::Matrix{Float64}\n\nNormalize matrix Ψ to have zero at minimum and 1.0 on the specified plasma boundary.\n\nReturns normalized matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.normalize_psi"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.psi_separation_z-Tuple{Content}","page":"API","text":"psi_separation_z(c::Content)\n\nThe Z coordinate to separate plasma and divertor areas with ψ ≤ 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.psi_separation_z"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.read_eqdsk-Tuple{IO}","page":"API","text":"read_eqdsk(io::IO)\n\nReads a stream according to spec found in G_EQDSK.pdf.\n\nreturns\n\n[`Content`](@ref)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.read_eqdsk"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.rpoints-Tuple{Content}","page":"API","text":"rpoints(c::Content)\n\nreturns\n\n    Coordinates of Ψ(r,z) along tokamak large radius R.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.rpoints"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#EQDSKReader.zpoints-Tuple{Content}","page":"API","text":"zpoints(c::Content)\n\nReturns  coordinates of Ψ(r,z) along tokamak vertial axis Z.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EQDSKReader.zpoints"},{"category":"section","location":"#EQDSKReader","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for EQDSKReader.\n\nPages = [\"index.md\", \"api.md\"]","title":"EQDSKReader"}]
